  "body": "OK, we have a spec!! This PR just cleans it up a bit. It might look like a lot of changes but none of the actual interesting content was really changed. It's more just guidance on how to write these sort of things, in pull request form. I hope it's educational. Please review it to let me know if anything is wrong.\n\nCommit message:\n\nThe main work here is clarifying the logger, formatter, and printer separation. They are now nested into their own section, and use function call notation to call each other. Printer was also factored out into its own section instead of being left vague.\n\nOther changes are minor editorial ones, e.g. changing capitalization or phrasing, or adding argument lists to the method headings.\n",
